  "production_change": {
    "contract": "RouterConfig::turn_entries: Option<usize>, the native equivalent of the existing optional JavaScript RouterConfig.turnEntries.",
    "constructor": "PolicyRouter::new applies Some(limit) to actual task and pending-attempt capacity; None retains1000.",
    "serialization": "None is omitted; Some uses camelCase turnEntries. CLI read_config initializes None and adds no environment/file setting.",
    "regression": "Definition6 configures capacity1 through the actual RouterConfig and checks rejected admission, unchanged counters and retained confirmed tool owner."
  },
  "adaptations": [
    "Native cancellation-free route options use owned strings and Option request IDs; absent prompt IDs use the same empty-string identity and omitted completion evidence uses Value::Null.",
    "Original JavaScript undefined configuration fields remain absent optional Rust fields. Default serialized configurations are checked by the existing core router-contract corpus.",
    "The advanced clock value in definition5 is retained. The frozen Node schedule actually reads its injected clock zero times because tasks remain active or pending; native boundary clock-read counts differ and are not asserted equivalent.",
    "Native mock implements the typed HTTP transport and returns the unchanged original confidence/tier JSON. No provider network calls, token-count function or classifier verdict stubs are used.",
    "Original internal record/attempt/tool-owner observations use the equivalent core TurnState accessors through the native router policy lock."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Definition5 proves active continuity under its advanced-clock schedule; it does not exercise a retired-task expiration branch or establish timing parity.",
    "The capture retains13 complete reference decisions and9 evaluator calls, but these additional fields are not all native differential assertions. Coverage rests on the19 original assertions and complete counterpart operation order.",
    "Focused native checks bind10 relevant inputs and a copied executable, not a full-workspace source-to-binary freeze. Concurrent buffered transport edits are separate.",
    "Initial scoped Clippy failed on two unrelated buffered-body style diagnostics. The failure is retained; subsequent strict runtime all-target Clippy passed after owner fixes.",
    "Integer Option<usize> is the typed Rust embedding contract; arbitrary JavaScript values outside valid capacity counts are not newly qualified.",
    "No full transport, provider, performance, platform, installed-archive or cutover gate is completed by this mapping."
  ],
